+
+Circular scrolling parameters
+=============================
+
+``AttrCircularScrollRingWidth`` is an unsigned, unitless setting from 1
+to 50, default 25. It specifies the outer percentage of the reported
+radius used as the circular ring. It does not depend on device resolution
+and must not be presented as a physical-distance measurement.
+
+``AttrCircularScrollDwell`` is the time, in milliseconds, a single contact
+must remain in the ring before circular scrolling arms. The default is
+300; accepted values are 0 through 2000. Moving into the pointer area or
+adding a finger cancels a pending ring contact. These attributes are used
+with ``ModelCircularTouchpad=1`` in a local device-quirk section. Circular
+mode retains normal two-finger horizontal and vertical scrolling and
+multi-finger gestures.
